      "math_academy_id": "q-23641",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d012a04e-f802-5a26-b900-0801427073d8",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $4{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡(2x).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the $4{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)$ from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡(2x) & =4{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)\\cdot (1+{cot}^{2}⁡(2x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)\\cdot (1+{cot}^{2}⁡(2x)) & =4{csc}^{2}⁡(2x)\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =4{csc}^{4}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
