    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-74574",
      "knowledge_point_id": "85555bce-debf-5165-ba6a-3c232deeeb0a",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ({csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)\\cancel{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
