    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-120321",
      "knowledge_point_id": "85555bce-debf-5165-ba6a-3c232deeeb0a",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta }.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the identity\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression and using the fact that $\\frac{1}{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta }={cot}^{3}⁡\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta } & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{3}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\,({csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
